Original plugin
---------------
Published by Mailwish — https://mailwish.com (GitHub org `mailwish`)
Branded Mailbux — https://mailbux.com (the repository's homepage field)
  SnappyMail CardDAV Auto, released 2025-11-12.
  Upstream repository: https://github.com/mailwish/SnappyMail-CardDAV-Plugin

  Upstream published this plugin without a licence file, and this fork does
  not add one: the terms are the original author's to set, not ours. The
  copyright in the original code is not ours — see the note at the end on
  which of the two names holds it. Anyone wanting to redistribute it should
  ask them. (The companion CalDAV plugin was released
  under MIT; that grant does not extend to this one.)

Fork maintainer
---------------
Fathi Ben Nasr <fbennasr@convergent.tn>
  Convergent Cloud Computing — https://www.convergent.tn
  Adaptations for standards compliance and interoperability with the
  Cyrus IMAP CardDAV implementation. See the commit history and README
  for the specific changes.

A note on the two names
-----------------------
The repository that published this plugin belongs to the **Mailwish** GitHub
organisation; its homepage field, its plugin name and its hardcoded service
host all say **Mailbux**. Both names are recorded here because both appear in
the original, and it is not ours to decide which one is the legal author.

On 15 August 2026 we wrote to support@mailbux.com about the missing licence and
our open pull requests (ticket #5577). Mailbux replied on 26 August:

    "Thank you for the kind words — but we think you may have the wrong
     maintainer. We do not publish or maintain SnappyMail plugins; our webmail
     work is based on a different stack, and we have no SnappyMail repositories.
     If you can send us the link to the repository where you found the plugins,
     we will gladly take a look and confirm either way."

The public contact of the organisation that holds the repositories is
support@mailwish.com, and that is where the question has been put next.

Until someone with authority states otherwise, nothing changes here: no licence
is added, the copyright is not ours, and anyone wanting to redistribute this
plugin should ask the original author. The plugin's entry in the SnappyMail
administration panel says so too, rather than inheriting the "AGPL v3" that
AbstractPlugin fills in by default — which would have claimed a grant nobody
ever made.
